# OffboardAGV — deregister a single AGV from the master. Wraps
# VDA5050Master::offboard_agv.
#
# Single-AGV variant. For offboarding multiple AGVs in one call, use
# OffboardAGVBatch.srv — the batch sibling.
#
# Request reuses AGVKey: the same {manufacturer, serial_number} identity
# pair used inside OffboardAGVBatch.srv batch requests.
#
# **What offboarding does master-side**:
#   - Removes the AGV from the master's onboard list.
#   - Calls AGV::stop(): unsubscribes from MQTT topics, drops the
#     outbound queue, joins the queue thread.
#   - Drops any active assignment_id correlation for this AGV.
#   - Subsequent service calls referencing this AGV (assign_order,
#     get_device_status, get_order_status, etc.) return AGV_NOT_ONBOARDED.
#
# **Idempotency**: offboarding a non-onboarded AGV returns NOT_ONBOARDED.
# FMS clients can call this safely without first checking onboarded state.

AGVKey agv
---
# Status enum.
#
# SUCCESS         — AGV successfully offboarded.
# NOT_ONBOARDED   — no AGV with this {manufacturer, serial_number} was
#                   found in the master's onboard list. Idempotent
#                   no-op; treat as success.
# INVALID_REQUEST — empty manufacturer or serial_number.
uint8 SUCCESS=0
uint8 NOT_ONBOARDED=1
uint8 INVALID_REQUEST=2
uint8 status

# Echo of request — async-fanout correlation.
string manufacturer
string serial_number
